Subject: winemac: hand the foreground back when the application is activated

macdrv_app_deactivated() gives the foreground window to the desktop and nothing
ever takes it back, so a process runs on with the desktop as its foreground for
the rest of its life. SSFIV pauses its intro movie when it loses focus -- correct
behaviour, and visible in quartz as IMediaControl::Pause -- and then never calls
Run, because the activation that should prompt it never reaches the game. The
movie stops on a frame, gstreamer backs up behind a filter that stopped
consuming, and the window is black until the game is killed.

Remember the window that was given up, and restore it on activation. winex11
needs neither half: its FocusIn event names the window that regained focus, and
focus_out() keeps a last_focus as a fallback for when that window cannot be
activated. macOS APP_ACTIVATED is process-wide and names nothing.

The record is kept in win32u state rather than asked of Cocoa. An earlier
attempt read [NSApp keyWindow] from applicationDidBecomeActive: and got the
window that was key BEFORE the switch, since AppKit posts that notification
before the newly clicked window becomes key; its fallback walked a keyWindows
list that is pruned only on close, so it could name a window no longer on
screen. Restoring goes through can_window_become_foreground(), the same gate
every other path to the foreground uses, and only when the foreground is still
the desktop -- a click that activates some other window arrives as its own
focus event and has already done the right thing.

The deactivation guard is replaced for a separate reason: it compared
get_active_window(), which is GUITHREADINFO for the CALLING thread, against the
global foreground window. APP_DEACTIVATED is handled by whichever thread pumps
events first, so the two matched only by luck.
---
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
@@ -1799,10 +1799,46 @@
  *
  * Handler for APP_ACTIVATED events.
  */
+/* The window this process gave up when macOS deactivated it, so activation can
+ * hand it back.
+ *
+ * winex11 never needs this: its FocusIn event names the window that regained
+ * focus, and focus_out() keeps a last_focus as a fallback when that window
+ * cannot be activated. macOS's APP_ACTIVATED is process-wide and names nothing,
+ * and macdrv_app_deactivated() below drops the foreground unconditionally --
+ * so without a record, nothing ever takes it back and the process runs on with
+ * the desktop as its foreground window for the rest of its life.
+ *
+ * Kept here rather than asked of Cocoa. An earlier version of this read
+ * [NSApp keyWindow] from applicationDidBecomeActive: and got the window that
+ * was key BEFORE the switch, because AppKit posts that notification before the
+ * newly clicked window becomes key; and its fallback walked a keyWindows list
+ * that is only pruned on close, so it could name a window no longer on screen.
+ * The foreground is win32u state, and this is win32u's side of it. */
+static HWND deactivated_foreground;
+
 void macdrv_app_activated(void)
 {
+    HWND hwnd = deactivated_foreground;
+
     TRACE("\n");
     macdrv_UpdateClipboard();
+
+    if (!hwnd) return;
+    deactivated_foreground = NULL;
+
+    /* The window may have been destroyed, hidden or disabled while we were in
+     * the background; can_window_become_foreground() is the same gate every
+     * other path to the foreground goes through. */
+    if (!can_window_become_foreground(hwnd)) return;
+
+    /* And something else may already have taken the foreground -- a click that
+     * activates a different window arrives as its own focus event, which has
+     * already done the right thing. Only restore what we ourselves cleared. */
+    if (NtUserGetForegroundWindow() != NtUserGetDesktopWindow()) return;
+
+    TRACE("restoring foreground window %p\n", hwnd);
+    NtUserSetForegroundWindowInternal(hwnd);
 }
 
 
@@ -1813,10 +1849,20 @@
  */
 void macdrv_app_deactivated(void)
 {
+    HWND foreground = NtUserGetForegroundWindow();
+    DWORD pid = 0;
+
     NtUserClipCursor(NULL);
 
-    if (get_active_window() == NtUserGetForegroundWindow())
+    /* The guard this replaces compared get_active_window() -- GUITHREADINFO for
+     * the CALLING thread -- against the global foreground window. APP_DEACTIVATED
+     * is process-wide and is handled by whichever thread pumps events first, so
+     * the two matched only when that thread happened to own the foreground.
+     * What matters is whether the foreground window is ours. */
+    if (foreground && NtUserGetWindowThread(foreground, &pid) &&
+        pid == GetCurrentProcessId())
     {
+        deactivated_foreground = foreground;
         TRACE("setting fg to desktop\n");
         NtUserSetForegroundWindowInternal(NtUserGetDesktopWindow());
     }
